{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1153393-send-large-object-to-the-shadow","id":1153393,"title":"Send large object to the shadow","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-26T21:55:04-07:00","id":1153393,"title":"Send large object to the shadow","content":"Hey team,<br /> <br /> I have a player that wants to send a large object to the shadow (over 1000lbs). He has spirit 4, no dots in the matter sphere.<br /> <br /> . First, is this possible?<br /> . If so, what would happen if the object had an active spirit?<br /> . Now that i am asking this. In mage it seems mages cross with everything (clothes, etc), but werewolves need to do a rite per object or go naked. Is this correct?<br /> <br /> We are using vanilla mage the awakening. But any feedback is appreciated!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1842-rluengo","name":"rluengo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T22:52:06-07:00","id":1153400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rluengo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1153393-send-large-object-to-the-shadow#post1153393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey team,<br /> <br /> I have a player that wants to send a large object to the shadow (over 1000lbs). He has spirit 4, no dots in the matter sphere.<br /> <br /> . First, is this possible?<br /> . If so, what would happen if the object had an active spirit?<br /> . Now that i am asking this. In mage it seems mages cross with everything (clothes, etc), but werewolves need to do a rite per object or go naked. Is this correct?<br /> <br /> We are using vanilla mage the awakening. But any feedback is appreciated!</div> </div> </div> </div>By vanilla do you mean 1e? 2e has the world walker spell that would work (taking into account size factors) and also has the 3 dot spell &quot;reaching&quot; to create a portal. 1e has &quot;Road Master&quot; that is similar. Both allow you to move things over into the shadow without using an Iris (portal) and also has the 3 dot version called &quot;spirit road&quot; to open a portal.<br /> <br /> Spirits arnt usually tethered to an object like ghosts with an anchor tho items that dont move might have spirits that cant move on their own. If its in the material world then its in probably also twilight and moving it into shadow just makes it be in the shadow like all the other spirits there.<br /> <br /> Anything going through a portal is turned into ephemera and usually directly teleporting into the shadow means everything the mage has on him also goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 10-27-2017, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T08:14:41-07:00","id":1153479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rluengo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1153393-send-large-object-to-the-shadow#post1153393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. Now that i am asking this. In mage it seems mages cross with everything (clothes, etc), but werewolves need to do a rite per object or go naked. Is this correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only in first edition (is that what you mean by vanilla?). In second edition they cross with everything they're carrying and wearing and stuff.<br /> <br /> What's the object, by the way? That might have more bearing on things.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T09:17:51-07:00","id":1153499,"title":"","content":"Hey team,<br /> <br /> Yes I meant 1e. The object is a large stone box (2m x 1m x 1m).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1842-rluengo","name":"rluengo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T09:22:49-07:00","id":1153503,"title":"","content":"Theoretically you just need to make a big portal. Might be difficult to push something that big and heavy through though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T09:27:34-07:00","id":1153505,"title":"","content":"I guess his question is whether he can touch it and send it there. Pushing is impossible for him (strength 2!). I do not think that should be a problem with Spirit 4, but not sure how it would work.<br /> <br /> Questions :<br /> <br /> What is there is a spirit for the stone box already? Would there be to &quot;box&quot; representations?<br /> Am I allowing something that is somehow stupid by the rules? (I know we can do anything of course, but always good to get people's opinion)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1842-rluengo","name":"rluengo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T10:10:06-07:00","id":1153521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rluengo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1153393-send-large-object-to-the-shadow?p=1153505#post1153505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess his question is whether he can touch it and send it there. Pushing is impossible for him (strength 2!). I do not think that should be a problem with Spirit 4, but not sure how it would work.<br /> <br /> Questions :<br /> <br /> What is there is a spirit for the stone box already? Would there be to &quot;box&quot; representations?<br /> Am I allowing something that is somehow stupid by the rules? (I know we can do anything of course, but always good to get people's opinion)</div> </div> </div> </div>oops didnt read the entire thread lol and missed it being 1e<br /> <br /> <sub>What edition are you talking about? In 2e you can use reach to move anything in sensory range into the shadow using spirit 4's world walker</sub>. It seems in 1e the road master spell only seems to let the mage transfer himself over and also get to decide what is able to go through the portals made with the 3 dot spirit road spell, but creative thaum should allow it easily enough.<br /> <br /> So yeh in 1e you open a portal big enough around the object so its enveloped by the portal and it should be fine. You really dont need to push it through the portal, creating one over/on it should be enough?<br /> <br /> Moving stuff into and out of the shadow is one of the things you use spirit to do so its not stupid and there are spells that allow you to do it in either edition.<br /> <br /> Remember that many spirits are spiritual reflections of material objects/emotions and can be separate from the material object they reflect even continuing to exist after the material object is gone. If a box has a spirit then the spirit probably cant move itself so will be in twilight as a separate entity from the box its a reflection off. So you have 2 things, a material box and a box spirit, both can be moved from one side of the gauntlet to the other using spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 10-27-2017, 02:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T10:20:53-07:00","id":1153524,"title":"","content":"Totalgit you are awesome!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1842-rluengo","name":"rluengo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T10:45:16-07:00","id":1153529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rluengo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1153393-send-large-object-to-the-shadow?p=1153524#post1153524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Totalgit you are awesome!</div> </div> </div> </div>If there is one thing this highlighted is that i now remember the gold text in 1e. Ugg, my eyes are sore just trying to read 1e again. But srsly <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1842-rluengo\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1842\" data-vbnamecard=\"1842\">rluengo</a> you should try get your group to update to 2e its much much cleaner system and i cant now ever think id want to run a 1e mage game over a 2e mage game ever again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T10:50:22-07:00","id":1153532,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, I do not like 2nd edition that much to be honest. I will use this 1e story to do a weird npc (2e) or something like that. Just to play with the new rules.<br /> <br /> I do not like how the conditions are designed, much less the experience system. Do not like the combat either :S. But again, might be because I have not tried it as much. On the other hand, I can see myself moving to classic instead! 20th anniversary is much more attractive to me at the moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1842-rluengo","name":"rluengo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}